*SPOILERS*

Ages ago, food was a real big problem which is one reason #pray was added.
If you play carefully  you won't ever have to worry about food again.

Assuming everything's good, here's what you do:

1) play normally until you are hungry
2) keep playing, but cautiously, until you become weak
3) #pray

bingo!  end of problem.

Okay, you got me...  it isn't quite that simple... but it almost is

The most important things are keeping you god happy, avoiding #pray
until your prayer time-out has expired, waiting until you are WEAK, NOT
hungry before praying, and maintaining at least non-negative luck.

How do I keep my god happy?  Easy, play carefully and avoid stupid mistakes.
-don't eat human corpses (dunno if this angers your god, but it should be
                          avoided anyway because of the aggrivate monste
                          intrinsic you'll acquire)
-don't kill your pet
-don't kill like-aligned, peacful creatures
-don't kill shopkeepers or priests(es)
-don't #pray before your prayer time-out has expired
-don't kick altars
-don't do anything which you think might PO your god

(seriously)
-don't do anything you think might PO your god

If you ever need to break one of the above:
-do set aside enough food to last until your god can be mollified
-do make sure you have a like-aligned altar handy

If you need to break both of the above:
-don't cry when you realize it was a mistake

It is possible to pray too often.  There is a prayer timeout, which
makes prayer a bad thing until it expires.  During the early stages,
prayer should only be used for getting your character out of jams.
You can pray for extra HP, AC, intrinsics later--after you get surplus
food and positive luck.  If you're constantly praying to get gifts,
you've got only yourself to blame when you die from something which
praying can cure: HP, starvation, turning to stone

There are lots of things you can do to make a praying life easier:
-carry around a couple food rations in case you need
 to wait for the time-out
-eat whenever you can to decrease the number of times you need to #pray
-pile extra food rations and other unnecessary equipment near staircases
-wait until FAINTING instead of WEAK if you are in a safe spot

Generally, avoid praying if you can, but don't hesitate to use it when
the need arises.  Now, after you've got 5 luck, plenty of food, and an
altar nearby, you don't need to be quite so careful-- go ahead, pray
then.

One other note about prayer is that Hand of Elbereth or Hand of Arioch
can be a death sentance for a starting character.  When you acquire either
of these, the prayer time-out (which generally expires about when you
become hungry) goes to something like 3000 turns.  This sucks the big one.
I don't reccommend getting a 10-13 luck since you could get HOE or HOA
by praying.  High level characters may prefer some of the intrinsics
to making prayer extremely difficult, but low level characters suffer
greatly.
